    description: "The profile's language breakdown and LOC totals, and the sketch Overview built from them, count tiers 1-2 only (ADR-0004 3a). Today profile.py (~line 985, language/LOC detection) counts every analysed file, and sketch.py _format_language_stats (~2838-2876) prints it: the 2026-10-14 self-sketch says \"Python (62%), C (26%)\", with C at 324,161 LOC -- almost all of it vendored tree-sitter-lean's 305,712-line generated parser.c. Agents reading the sketch are told hypergumbo is a quarter C.\n\nUse a path-only tier check (supply_chain patterns; no file reads) per language bucket, so the profile stays cheap; percentages over tiers 1-2. Tier-3 totals are kept and disclosed by the disclosure-line item, not dropped. Accepted cost (ADR text): a first-party directory literally named vendor/ below the root (already tier 3, supply_chain.py ~577) also leaves the language line, visibly, because the disclosure names it.\n\nEvidence at close: self-sketch Overview shows no C line; tier-3 node count unchanged (174 on 2026-10-15)."  # a0e6
    fields: {}  # a0e6
