  message: "Fixed in PR #1614 (fd6005c7da). profile.languages[L] gains own_files/own_loc (tier 1-2 by the new path-only supply_chain.tier_by_path, sharing classify_file's DERIVED_*/EXTERNAL_DEP_* helpers); files/loc unchanged so analyzers still run on vendored code. Sketch Overview language line, file and LOC totals read the own share; its test count skips vendored tests. Evidence: test_language_stats_count_own_code_only (profile with C loc 3000/own 100 renders 'Python (90%), C (10%)', totals 11 files / ~1,000 LOC), test_detect_languages_counts_own_code_separately (vendor/grammar/parser.c in files, not own_*). On this repo, tier_by_path over git ls-files: 11 C/H files, 325,450 lines, own 0 -> no C line; Python 1684 files / own 1683. NOT run: a self-sketch (big repo; not authorised this session), so the item's 'self-sketch Overview shows no C line' is shown by the path measurement and the formatter test, not a live sketch. Gap noted: ADR-0004 3a also lists 'which linkers count as active'; linker activation still reads profile.languages keys (no item covers it)."  # 6b7b
